/**
 * Recalculates Account.Rating from the account's open pipeline:
 *
 *   Hot  - at least one open opportunity with Amount >= 100,000
 *   Warm - open opportunities, but none with Amount >= 100,000
 *   Cold - no open opportunities
 *
 * Runs asynchronously (@future) so opportunity saves stay fast, and is
 * bulk-safe: it accepts a Set of AccountIds so a single future call can
 * cover an entire CPQ batch (the per-transaction async-call limit is 50).
 */
public inherited sharing class AccountRatingService {

    /** Amount threshold that makes an account Hot. */
    private static final Decimal HOT_AMOUNT_THRESHOLD = 100000;
    /** Rating picklist values. */
    private static final String RATING_HOT = 'Hot';
    private static final String RATING_WARM = 'Warm';
    private static final String RATING_COLD = 'Cold';

    /**
     * Async entry point called from the Opportunity trigger.
     * One call per transaction with the full set of affected AccountIds.
     */
    @future
    public static void recalculate(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // One aggregate query covers the whole batch:
        // MAX(Amount) ignores nulls, so an account whose open opps all
        // lack an Amount still counts as open (Warm).
        Map<Id, Decimal> maxOpenAmountByAccount = new Map<Id, Decimal>();
        for (AggregateResult ar : [
            SELECT AccountId accountId, MAX(Amount) maxAmount
            FROM Opportunity
            WHERE AccountId IN :accountIds
              AND IsClosed = false
            GROUP BY AccountId
        ]) {
            maxOpenAmountByAccount.put(
                (Id) ar.get('accountId'),
                (Decimal) ar.get('maxAmount')
            );
        }

        List<Account> accountsToUpdate = new List<Account>();

        for (Id accountId : accountIds) {
            String newRating;

            if (!maxOpenAmountByAccount.containsKey(accountId)) {
                newRating = RATING_COLD;
            } else if (maxOpenAmountByAccount.get(accountId) >= HOT_AMOUNT_THRESHOLD) {
                newRating = RATING_HOT;
            } else {
                newRating = RATING_WARM;
            }

            accountsToUpdate.add(new Account(
                Id = accountId,
                Rating = newRating
            ));
        }

        // Skip DML entirely when nothing actually changed, to avoid
        // redundant saves and downstream automation churn.
        Map<Id, Account> existingAccounts = new Map<Id, Account>([
            SELECT Id, Rating
            FROM Account
            WHERE Id IN :accountIds
        ]);

        List<Account> changedAccounts = new List<Account>();
        for (Account acc : accountsToUpdate) {
            Account existing = existingAccounts.get(acc.Id);
            if (existing == null || existing.Rating != acc.Rating) {
                changedAccounts.add(acc);
            }
        }

        if (!changedAccounts.isEmpty()) {
            // Partial-success DML so one bad record doesn't sink the batch.
            Database.update(changedAccounts, false);
        }
    }
}
```

**Notes on correctness and limits:**
- The trigger fires `after insert`/`after update`, so `AccountId` is committed and the async job always sees a valid parent (no `UNABLE_TO_LOCK_ROW`/lookup-missing race from a `before` trigger).
- The `@future` context gets its own set of limits — a 200-row CPQ batch maps to at most 200 affected accounts, well within the 50,000-row query limit of a single future call.
- Filtering the trigger to `StageName`/`Amount`/parent changes (rather than firing on every update) keeps future-call usage minimal.
- One thing to watch: because this is `@future`, the Rating update lands milliseconds after the opportunity save, not inside it. If anyone ever needs it synchronous (e.g., a report pulled immediately after save), `Queueable` with `Database.Stateful` or chaining the same logic synchronously from the trigger would be the upgrade path — but `@future` matches what you asked for and keeps saves fastest.

